---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Gallery from '../components/Gallery.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import { projectsIn } from '../lib/media';
import { serviceSchema, breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/kendall-pergolas/';
const title = 'Pergolas Kendall FL | Patio Covers & Pool Structures';
const description =
  'Pergolas in Kendall — extending established patios, working around existing screen enclosures and pool cages, and replacing timber structures that have had their day.';

const crumbs = [{ href: '/service-areas/', label: 'Service Areas' }, { label: 'Kendall' }];

const schema = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Pergola design and installation in Kendall, Florida',
    description,
    path,
    serviceType: 'Pergola construction',
    areaServed: ['Kendall, Florida', 'Miami-Dade County, Florida'],
    offers: ['Custom pergolas', 'Attached patio covers', 'Pergola replacement', 'Screen enclosure extensions'],
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, path),
  webPageSchema({ path, name: title, description }),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} crumbs={crumbs} schema={schema}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Kendall"
    title="Pergolas in Kendall, Working With What Is Already There"
    lede="Kendall is established. Most of the houses have been there for decades, most of the yards have mature planting, and a very large number of them already have something out back — a screened pool enclosure, a slab that was poured for a patio, or a timber structure that has quietly reached the end of its life. Building here is usually about extending or replacing rather than starting from nothing."
    facts={[
      { label: 'Typical lot', value: 'Established home, mature landscaping, existing patio or enclosure' },
      { label: 'Typical build', value: 'Attached covers, enclosure extensions and replacements' },
      { label: 'Design driver', value: 'Tying cleanly into what is already on the property' },
      { label: 'Frequent job', value: 'Replacing failed timber structures' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Screen enclosures and pool cages</h2>
      <p>
        A large share of Kendall homes have a screened pool enclosure, and that is the single
        biggest factor in how a new structure gets designed. There are three workable
        approaches, and which one applies depends on the cage and on what you actually want.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Build clear of it.</strong> A freestanding structure set outside the enclosure
        footprint, giving you a genuinely open, unscreened space beside the caged pool. This
        is often the best of both — screened swimming, open dining.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Extend beyond it.</strong> A covered area picking up where the cage ends,
        usually attached to the house, with the tie-in detailed so water sheds away from both
        the wall and the enclosure frame rather than into the junction.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Replace part of it.</strong> Where a cage is aging, removing a section and
        putting a solid-roofed structure in its place gives you a dry, usable outdoor room
        instead of a screened one. That is a bigger job and worth discussing honestly before
        anyone commits to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Replacing a timber structure that has gone</h2>
      <p>
        Wood pergolas built in Kendall twenty or thirty years ago are, in a great many cases,
        now due. The signs are consistent: soft posts at the base, split beams around
        fixings, a roof that never really shed water, and a general sagging that no amount of
        re-staining fixes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Replacement is straightforward work and a good moment to reconsider the material. If
        the spot is under mature canopy and out of the direct sun, timber remains a legitimate
        choice — see the honest version of that argument on the{' '}
        <a href="/pergolas/wood/">wood pergolas page</a>. If it sits in the open, this is the
        moment to move to{' '}
        <a href="/pergolas/aluminum/">aluminium</a> and stop the maintenance cycle for good.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will tell you plainly whether what you have is worth repairing or whether you are
        better off starting again. Sometimes the frame is sound and only the roof needs
        replacing, which is a much smaller job than most people expect.
      </p>

      <h2>Mature landscaping changes the design</h2>
      <p>
        Established Kendall yards usually have real trees, and that is an advantage worth
        designing around rather than removing. Existing canopy takes the edge off the sun,
        which opens up material options and often means a smaller structure does the job.
      </p>
      <p>
        The practical constraint is roots. Mature root systems rule out footing positions the
        same way pool plumbing does, and they are found on the site visit rather than on the
        morning of the dig. Overhanging branches also matter for a{' '}
        <a href="/tiki-huts/">thatched roof</a>, where constant leaf litter shortens the life
        of the thatch considerably.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-sand">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our work</p>
        <h2>Structures built around existing pools and decks</h2>
      </div>
      <Gallery projects={projectsIn('pergolas')} limit={2} />
      <p style="margin-top:var(--space-l)">
        <a class="btn btn-dark" href="/gallery/">See every project</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell form-band">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Get a pergola quote in Kendall</h2>
        <p>
          If there is already a structure or an enclosure out back, photograph it from
          underneath as well as from the yard — that is what shows whether a frame is sound.
          Rough dimensions and which way the back of the house faces complete the picture.
        </p>
        <p>
          Also see <a href="/miami-pergolas/">Miami</a>,{' '}
          <a href="/homestead-pergolas/">Homestead</a> and the full{' '}
          <a href="/service-areas/">service areas list</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <QuoteForm service="Pergola" city="Kendall" compact />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Extending, replacing, or starting fresh?"
    body="Send photographs of what is there now. Half the answer is usually visible in them."
    secondaryLabel="Pergola options"
    secondaryHref="/pergolas/"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .form-band { display: grid; gap: var(--space-l); }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .form-band { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: var(--space-2xl); align-items: start; }
  }
</style>
